Since CD is perpendicular to AB (the x-axis) at point M, which is the midpoint of CD. Let me denote the x-coordinate of M as m. Then, since CD is vertical, the points C and D will have coordinates (m, k) and (m, -k) for some k, because M is the midpoint, so the y-coordinates are k and -k. The length of CD is then 2k. Since CD is a chord of the circle, these points must satisfy the circle equation.

